From 8bd09d0aeca826bcd6d22214fb102bab026a26e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theldus <davidsondfgl@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 5 Sep 2021 17:33:49 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Nano v2.7.2 support

This patch brings Nano v2.7.2 support to Nanvix.

This patch applies the following modifications:
- Add Nanvix to target list
- Add pdcurses as the library to be linked
- Fixes missing headers (strings.h)
- Change lstat to stat, since Nanvix doesn't support lstat.
  Importantly, there are almost no symlinks in the file system, I
  wouldn't say this is a concern.
- Switches the use of methods like getpwent() to getenv("HOME") in
  the '~' resolution, since Nanvix doesn't supports these methods.
- Disables linter, since 'undefined reference' occurs during builds.
- Disable reading via stdin, this adds complexity to the code that I
  don't want to have to deal with.
- Change all calls from sigaction to signal, since Nanvix doesn't
  support sigaction, and I'm too lazy to think about adding support.
- Remove call to set_escdelay, as PDCurses does not support.
- Removes the use of gobbling, as Nanvix doesn't support it either.
  Because of this, files read via 'include' (inside nanorc) must
  contain the full path. Credits to the Sortix patch since I based
  on it.

  Recommended build flags:
  CFLAGS="-DDISABLE_LINTER" ./configure --host=i386-elf-nanvix \
    --enable-tiny --disable-nls --enable-color --enable-nanorc \
	--prefix="/" --enable-linenumbers
